This project is a content-based movie recommendation system built in Python that suggests movies similar to a selected title using metadata such as genres, keywords, cast, crew, and overview. It combines two TMDb datasets, tmdb_5000_movies.csv and tmdb_5000_credits.csv, into a unified dataset, which is cleaned and preprocessed to remove missing values and duplicates. Important features are extracted and combined into a single 'tags' column, which is processed with stemming using NLTK and converted into numerical vectors using CountVectorizer. Cosine similarity is calculated to recommend the top 5 movies most similar to the chosen title. The processed dataset is saved using pickle for quick and efficient future use, making the system easy to extend with user ratings, web interfaces, or advanced NLP techniques.
